[asy]
draw( (0,0) -- (4,0) -- (4,1) -- (0,1) -- cycle);draw( (2,0) -- (0,1) ); draw( (4,0) -- (0,1));
fill( (0,0) -- (0,1) -- (2,0) -- cycle, gray); fill( (0,1) -- (4,0) -- (4,1) -- cycle, gray);
label("$A$", (0,1) , NW); label("$B$", (0,0) , SW); label("$C$", (4,0) , SE);label("$D$", (4,1) , NE);label("$E$", (2,0), S);
[/asy]

Solve the problem, showing your work. Put the final answer in \boxed{}.

Circles with centers $A$ and $B$ have radii  3 and 8, respectively. A common internal tangent touches the circles at $C$ and $D$, as shown. Lines $AB$ and $CD$ intersect at $E$, and $AE = 5$. What is $CD$?

[asy]
unitsize(0.2cm);
pair A,B,C,D,E;
A=(0,0);
B=(18.3,0);
E=(5,0);
C=(1.8,-2.4);
D=(13.5,6.4);
draw(Circle(A,3),linewidth(0.7));
draw(Circle(B,8),linewidth(0.7));
draw(A--B,linewidth(0.7));
draw(C--D,linewidth(0.7));
label("$A$",A,W);
label("$B$",B,S);
label("$C$",C,S);
label("$D$",D,NW);
label("$E$",E,S);
[/asy]

Solve the problem, showing your work. Put the final answer in \boxed{}.

records.scion_answer:
The radical conjugate of an expression of the form $a + b\sqrt{c}$ is $a - b\sqrt{c}$.

So the radical conjugate of $5 - 6\sqrt{2}$ is $5 + 6\sqrt{2}$.

\boxed{5 + 6\sqrt{2}}
